:HELP NAME=ADDLNK.Add Link (ADDLNK)
:P.The Add Link (ADDLNK) command works with a symbolic or hard link to
an object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLNK/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLNK/NEWLNK'.New link (NEWLNK)
:P.The new link for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLNK/LNKTYPE'.Link type (LNKTYPE)
:P.The link type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYMBOLIC, *HARD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDMFS.Add Mounted FS (ADDMFS)
:P.Use the Add Mounted FS (ADDMFS) command to mount a file system over a
directory (MOUNT's twin).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/TYPE'.Type of file system (TYPE)
:P.The type of file system for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NFS, *UDFS, *NETWORK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/MFS'.File system to mount (MFS)
:P.The file system to mount&colon. a user-defined file system path or a
network file system export.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/MNTOVRDIR'.Directory to mount over (MNTOVRDIR)
:P.The directory the file system is mounted over.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/OPTIONS'.Mount options (OPTIONS)
:P.The mount options for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2048 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given,
'rw,suid,retry=5,rsize=32768,wsize=32768,timeo=20,retrans=5,acregmin=30,acregmax=60,acdirmin=30,acdirmax=60,hard'
is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *BINARY is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMFS/CODEPAGE'.Code page (CODEPAGE)
:P.The code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *BINARY is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CD.Change Current Directory (CD)
:P.Use the Change Current Directory (CD) command to change the job's
current directory (CHGCURDIR's alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CD/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGATR.Change Attribute (CHGATR)
:P.Use the Change Attribute (CHGATR) command to change one attribute of
IFS objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/ATR'.Attribute (ATR)
:P.The attribute for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID determines the conversion.
:PT.:PK.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *READONLY, *HIDDEN, *PCSYSTEM, *PCARCHIVE,
*SYSARCHIVE, *ALWCKPWRT, *USECOUNT, *DISKSTGOPT, *MAINSTGOPT,
*CRTOBJSCAN, *SCAN, *ALWSAV, *RSTDRNMUNL, *SETUID, *SETGID, *CRTOBJAUD,
*INHCKPWRT, *RUNEXIT, *CRTRUNEXIT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/VALUE'.New value (VALUE)
:P.The new value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:PT.:PK.*CHGONLY:EPK.
:PD.Changes only.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RESET, *MINIMIZE, *DYNAMIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/SYMLNK'.Symbolic link (SYMLNK)
:P.Whether to symbolic link.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGATR/TEXT'.Text description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGCURDIR.Change Current Directory (CHGCURDIR)
:P.Use the Change Current Directory (CHGCURDIR) command to change the
job's current directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCURDIR/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHKIN.Check In Object (CHKIN)
:P.Use the Check In Object (CHKIN) command to check an IFS object back
in.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKIN/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKIN/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHKOUT.Check Out Object (CHKOUT)
:P.Use the Check Out Object (CHKOUT) command to check an IFS object out;
others may read it only.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKOUT/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKOUT/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPY.Copy Object (CPY)
:P.Use the Copy Object (CPY) command to copy objects, a directory's
contents with SUBTREE(*ALL).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/TODIR'.To directory (TODIR)
:P.The to directory for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '.' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/TOOBJ'.To object (TOOBJ)
:P.The to object for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/SYMLNK'.Symbolic link (SYMLNK)
:P.Whether to symbolic link.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/FROMCCSID'.From CCSID (FROMCCSID)
:P.The CCSID the data is in.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/TOCCSID'.To CCSID (TOCCSID)
:P.The to CCSID for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/DTAFMT'.Data format (DTAFMT)
:P.The format of the data&colon. fixed-length fields or delimited.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PK.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NODIR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/REPLACE'.Replace object (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/OWNER'.Owner (OWNER)
:P.The owner of the objects created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ, *INDIROBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/FROMCODPAG'.From code page (FROMCODPAG)
:P.The from code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPY/TOCODEPAGE'.To code page (TOCODEPAGE)
:P.The to code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYFRMSTMF.Copy From Stream File (CPYFRMSTMF)
:P.Use the Copy From Stream File (CPYFRMSTMF) command to copy a stream
file's lines into a database member.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/FROMSTMF'.Stream file to read (FROMSTMF)
:P.The stream file to read for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/TOMBR'.Member path to write (TOMBR)
:P.The member of the to-file that receives the data.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/MBROPT'.When the member exists (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/CVTDTA'.Data conversion (CVTDTA)
:P.The data conversion for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TBL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/STMFCCSID'.Stream file data CCSID (STMFCCSID)
:P.The stream file data CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/DBFCCSID'.Member data CCSID (DBFCCSID)
:P.The member data CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/TBL'.Conversion table path (TBL)
:P.The conversion table path for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/ENDLINFMT'.Line ends read (ENDLINFMT)
:P.The line ends read for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CRLF:EPK.
:PD.Carriage return and line feed.
:PT.:PK.*LF:EPK.
:PD.Line feed.
:PT.:PK.*CR:EPK.
:PD.Carriage return.
:PT.:PK.*FIXED:EPK.
:PD.Fixed length.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LFCR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/TABEXPN'.Tabs to blanks (TABEXPN)
:P.Whether to tabs to blanks.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMSTMF/STMFCODPAG'.Stream file code page (STMFCODPAG)
:P.The stream file code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYTOSTMF.Copy To Stream File (CPYTOSTMF)
:P.Use the Copy To Stream File (CPYTOSTMF) command to copy a database
member's records into a stream file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/FROMMBR'.Member path to copy (FROMMBR)
:P.The member the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/TOSTMF'.Stream file to write (TOSTMF)
:P.The stream file to write for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/STMFOPT'.When the stream file exists (STMFOPT)
:P.The when the stream file exists for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/CVTDTA'.Data conversion (CVTDTA)
:P.The data conversion for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TBL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/DBFCCSID'.Member data CCSID (DBFCCSID)
:P.The member data CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/STMFCCSID'.Stream file data CCSID (STMFCCSID)
:P.The stream file data CCSID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/TBL'.Conversion table path (TBL)
:P.The conversion table path for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/ENDLINFMT'.Line end written (ENDLINFMT)
:P.The line end written for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CRLF:EPK.
:PD.Carriage return and line feed.
:PT.:PK.*LF:EPK.
:PD.Line feed.
:PT.:PK.*CR:EPK.
:PD.Carriage return.
:PT.:PK.*FIXED:EPK.
:PD.Fixed length.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LFCR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/AUT'.Authority of a new file (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INDIRFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOSTMF/STMFCODPAG'.Stream file code page (STMFCODPAG)
:P.The stream file code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*STMF:EPK.
:PD.A stream file.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTDIR.Create Directory (CRTDIR)
:P.Use the Create Directory (CRTDIR) command to make a directory (MD and
MKDIR are the same command).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/DTAAUT'.Public authority for data (DTAAUT)
:P.The data authorities&colon. read, add, update, delete and execute.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RWX, *RW, *RX, *WX, *R, *W, *X.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/OBJAUT'.Public authority for object (OBJAUT)
:P.The object authorities&colon. operational, management, existence,
alter and reference.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INDIR:EPK.
:PD.The authority comes from the directory the object is in.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/CRTOBJAUD'.Auditing value for objects (CRTOBJAUD)
:P.The auditing value given to objects created in the library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/CRTOBJSCAN'.Scanning option for objects (CRTOBJSCAN)
:P.Whether objects created in the library are scanned by the exit
programs of the scan exit points.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*CHGONLY:EPK.
:PD.Changes only.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PARENT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDIR/RSTDRNMUNL'.Restricted rename and unlink (RSTDRNMUNL)
:P.Whether renaming and unlinking objects in the directory is restricted
to their owners.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTUDFS.Create User-Defined FS (CRTUDFS)
:P.Use the Create User-Defined FS (CRTUDFS) command to make a
user-defined file system, /dev/QASPnn/NAME.udfs.
