:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MOUNT.Add Mounted FS (MOUNT)
:P.Use the Add Mounted FS (MOUNT) command to mount a file system over a
directory (ADDMFS is the same).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/TYPE'.Type of file system (TYPE)
:P.The type of file system for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NFS, *UDFS, *NETWORK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/MFS'.File system to mount (MFS)
:P.The file system to mount&colon. a user-defined file system path or a
network file system export.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/MNTOVRDIR'.Directory to mount over (MNTOVRDIR)
:P.The directory the file system is mounted over.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/OPTIONS'.Mount options (OPTIONS)
:P.The mount options for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2048 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given,
'rw,suid,retry=5,rsize=32768,wsize=32768,timeo=20,retrans=5,acregmin=30,acregmax=60,acdirmin=30,acdirmax=60,hard'
is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *BINARY is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOUNT/CODEPAGE'.Code page (CODEPAGE)
:P.The code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, *BINARY is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MOV.Move Object (MOV)
:P.Use the Move Object (MOV) command to move objects to another
directory or name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/TODIR'.To directory (TODIR)
:P.The to directory for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '.' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/TOOBJ'.To object (TOOBJ)
:P.The to object for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/FROMCCSID'.From CCSID (FROMCCSID)
:P.The CCSID the data is in.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/TOCCSID'.To CCSID (TOCCSID)
:P.The to CCSID for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCCSID:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65533.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/DTAFMT'.Data format (DTAFMT)
:P.The format of the data&colon. fixed-length fields or delimited.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BINARY:EPK.
:PD.Binary&colon. no conversion.
:PT.:PK.*TEXT:EPK.
:PD.Text.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/FROMCODPAG'.From code page (FROMCODPAG)
:P.The from code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MOV/TOCODEPAGE'.To code page (TOCODEPAGE)
:P.The to code page for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*STDASCII:EPK.
:PD.The standard ASCII CCSID.
:PT.:PK.*PCASCII:EPK.
:PD.The CCSID of the ASCII code page of personal computers.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RCLLNK.Reclaim Object Links (RCLLNK)
:P.Use the Reclaim Object Links (RCLLNK) command to reclaim the
IFS&colon. attributes, owners, authorities, links.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLLNK/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLLNK/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DIR:EPK.
:PD.The directory and the objects in it, but not its subdirectories'
contents.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLLNK/DMGOBJOPT'.Damaged object option (DMGOBJOPT)
:P.The damaged object option for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object option
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:PT.:PK.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Unusable directory option
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:PT.:PK.*KEEP:EPK.
:PD.Kept.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RD.Remove Directory (RD)
:P.Use the Remove Directory (RD) command to remove a directory (RMDIR's
alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RD/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RD/SUBTREE'.Remove subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RD/RMVLNK'.Remove links in directory (RMVLNK)
:P.Whether to remove links in directory.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=REN.Rename Object (REN)
:P.Use the Rename Object (REN) command to rename an object link (RNM's
alias).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='REN/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='REN/NEWOBJ'.New object name (NEWOBJ)
:P.The new object name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMDIR.Remove Directory (RMDIR)
:P.Use the Remove Directory (RMDIR) command to remove a directory (RD is
the same command).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMDIR/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMDIR/SUBTREE'.Remove subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMDIR/RMVLNK'.Remove links in directory (RMVLNK)
:P.Whether to remove links in directory.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVLNK.Remove Link (RMVLNK)
:P.Use the Remove Link (RMVLNK) command to remove a link; a pattern in
the last name removes each match.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVLNK/OBJLNK'.Object link (OBJLNK)
:P.The object link for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVMFS.Remove Mounted FS (RMVMFS)
:P.Use the Remove Mounted FS (RMVMFS) command to unmount a file system
(UNMOUNT's twin).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMFS/TYPE'.Type of file system (TYPE)
:P.The type of file system for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NFS, *UDFS, *NETWORK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMFS/MNTOVRDIR'.Directory mounted over (MNTOVRDIR)
:P.The directory the file system is mounted over.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MFS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMFS/MFS'.Mounted file system (MFS)
:P.The file system to mount&colon. a user-defined file system path or a
network file system export.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RNM.Rename Object (RNM)
:P.Use the Rename Object (RNM) command to give an object link a new name
in its directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNM/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNM/NEWOBJ'.New object name (NEWOBJ)
:P.The new object name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVCURDIR.Retrieve Current Directory (RTVCURDIR)
:P.The Retrieve Current Directory (RTVCURDIR) command works with the
job's current directory into CL variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCURDIR/RTNDIR'.CL var for current directory (RTNDIR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of current directory. Give a
character variable of at least 5000 characters.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCURDIR/DIRNAMLEN'.CL var for directory length (DIRNAMLEN)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of directory length. Give a
decimal variable of 7 digits, 0 after the point.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=UNMOUNT.Remove Mounted FS (UNMOUNT)
:P.Use the Remove Mounted FS (UNMOUNT) command to unmount a file system
(RMVMFS is the same command).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UNMOUNT/TYPE'.Type of file system (TYPE)
:P.The type of file system for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NFS, *UDFS, *NETWORK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UNMOUNT/MNTOVRDIR'.Directory mounted over (MNTOVRDIR)
:P.The directory the file system is mounted over.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MFS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='UNMOUNT/MFS'.Mounted file system (MFS)
:P.The file system to mount&colon. a user-defined file system path or a
network file system export.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKLNK.Work with Object Links (WRKLNK)
:P.The Work with Object Links (WRKLNK) command works with the links a
path names, with options to work on them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLNK/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLNK/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
